# Savanti Romero's X is "the number of counters on" it, of any kind. Bot1 casts it on turn 1 and then Rapier Wit on it: on Bot1's own
# turn the tapped creature gets a stun counter. At the beginning of combat it gets a +1/+1 counter, so there are two counters on it, one
# of each kind, and X is 2: Bot1 draws 2 (the 1 card Rapier Wit drew, plus 2) and loses 2 (life 18). Counting only the +1/+1 counters
# would draw and lose 1.

